    {
      "id": "03-create",
      "instruction": "In Odoo, go to the Sales app and create a new quotation. Set the Customer field to '{{runid}} Bench Customer' — this is an autocomplete dropdown, so type the name and actually click the matching option in the dropdown that appears (the value only counts if chosen from the dropdown). Then in the Order Lines table, add ONE order line: pick any product from the product catalogue (again an autocomplete dropdown — type and click the option that appears), and set the quantity to 3. Let Odoo fill in the unit price automatically. Then report: (a) the exact product name you chose, (b) the unit price the app filled in for that line, and (c) the Untaxed Amount shown in the quotation's totals. Do not save/confirm the quotation yet — just leave it as a draft quotation with that one line, but make sure the totals are visible. Do not wait for network idle; wait on concrete page state instead.",
