    {
      "id": "05-open",
      "instruction": "In Odoo, on the currently open draft quotation form for customer '{{runid}} Bench Customer' (unsaved, one order line: {{03-create.product_name}}, qty {{03-create.quantity}}, unit price {{03-create.unit_price}}, Untaxed Amount {{03-create.untaxed_amount}}). Task: give the quotation a SECOND order line with a DIFFERENT product, quantity 2. Steps: (1) If any notification/toast banner is visible on the page, dismiss it (click its close X) so it cannot intercept clicks. (2) Click Save so the quotation is saved as a draft and gets a reference name (e.g. S000xx) — report that name from the breadcrumb. (3) Click 'Add a line' in the Order Lines table to create a new row, click into the new row's Product cell, type a product name (e.g. 'Customizable Desk' or 'Desk'), wait for the autocomplete dropdown options to render, then choose an option: click it with a real mouse click at its center; if afterwards the row's Unit Price cell is still {{04-open.line2_unit_price}}, retry with keyboard: focus the product input, type the name, press ArrowDown once then Enter. Keep trying until the product actually commits — the row's Unit Price cell must fill with a non-zero value and the Subtotal cell must show a non-zero amount. (4) Set that row's Quantity to 2. (5) Click somewhere neutral outside the table (e.g. the quotation title area) to commit the row, and verify the Untaxed Amount in the totals changed from {{03-create.untaxed_amount}}. (6) Click Save. Report: (a) quotation reference name from breadcrumb, (b) exact product name of the second line, (c) its unit price, (d) the new Untaxed Amount, (e) both lines' product/qty/unit price/subtotal as shown. Do NOT confirm the quotation (leave it in draft). Do not wait for network idle; wait on concrete page state instead.",
